 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`. I only parsed a program with the attribute and checked the resulting `DefFrame`. I did not test stringifying it, and I did not run the test suite.\n\n- **Class:** `DefFrame` has a new optional `channel_delay` field.\n- **Stringification:** `DefFrame.out()` includes `CHANNEL-DELAY` when the field is set.\n- **Parsing:** the grammar accepts `CHANNEL-DELAY` as a frame attribute. The parser maps it to `channel_delay`.\n- **Reserved word:** I added `CHANNEL-DELAY` to the `RESERVED_WORDS` list in `quilbase.py`, next to `INITIAL-FREQUENCY`.\n\nThe check was a program with `DEFFRAME 0 \"x\":` followed by `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-7`. That parsed, and the `DefFrame` came back with `channel_delay=1e-07`.\n\nThe changes are in `pyquil/quilbase.py`, `pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark` and `pyquil/_parser/parser.py`. I haven't committed anything.",
